From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orangepi6 kernel-7 port
Subject: [PATCH] misc armchina npu drop IRQF_ONESHOT from non threaded irq

The NPU requests a plain hard IRQ (its bottom half is a workqueue) with
IRQF_ONESHOT set. 7.x warns once in __setup_irq() about ONESHOT without a
thread handler. Drop the flag; behaviour is unchanged.
---
 drivers/misc/armchina-npu/aipu_irq.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/aipu_irq.c b/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/aipu_irq.c
index a4bad6e2f..9a9a614b3 100755
--- a/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/aipu_irq.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/aipu_irq.c
@@ -63,12 +63,12 @@ struct aipu_irq_object *aipu_create_irq_object(struct device *dev, u32 irqnum, v
 
 	INIT_WORK(&irq_obj->work, aipu_irq_handler_bottom_half);
 
-	/**
-	 * Flag IRQF_ONESHOT is used when sharing interrupts with other devices using thread_irq.
-	 * Remove it if you have no such a usage scenario.
+	/*
+	 * No threaded handler is used (the bottom half is a workqueue), so
+	 * IRQF_ONESHOT has no meaning here and newer kernels warn about it.
 	 */
 	ret = request_irq(irqnum, aipu_irq_handler_upper_half,
-			  IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_PROBE_SHARED,
+			  IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_PROBE_SHARED,
 			  description, irq_obj->dev);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "request_irq failed: irqnum %u, ret %d", irqnum, ret);
